ts for  producers and less financial incentives  for industry's biggest players it's  getting driven by the big companies are  supplying the material but you know the  garden centers they're they're buying  all these different things to put put to  the public - by the garden center should  be taking more responsibility  the department for the environment told  us that amateur gardeners should play  their part by switching to peat free  alternatives but environmentalists  believe it's up to the government to put  more pressure on suppliers to ensure  that Pete doesn't get put in a bag but  stays in a bog Caterina potosi Sky News  in Cumbria
 

